# Line-ending policy.
#
# This file is committed, so it travels with the repo and OVERRIDES whatever
# core.autocrlf each machine happens to have set. That is the point: both of
# Scott's machines, and any fresh clone, agree without local configuration.

# Everything text: LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
# Not just "LF when committed" — eol=lf also stops checkout rewriting to CRLF,
# which is what keeps WSL happy, since /mnt/d files are the same files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Determinism-critical data: NEVER translate.
#
# The Phase 6 replay test compares golden logs BYTE FOR BYTE — that comparison
# is the evidence for the project's central claim that the core is
# deterministic. A line-ending conversion anywhere in that path produces diffs
# that have nothing to do with the engine, and it would show up intermittently
# (after a fresh clone, or on one machine only), which is the worst possible
# failure mode for the one test whose job is to be trustworthy.
#
# `-text` disables eol conversion but keeps textual diffs readable, which
# `binary` would not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.golden        -text
tests/golden/** -text
tests/data/**   -text

# Scripts must be LF or Linux refuses them: /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter
*.sh text eol=lf

# Genuinely binary
*.exe binary
*.o   binary
*.obj binary
